        "correct": 3,
        "explanation": "Competitive inhibitors bind to the active site, competing with substrate. This increases the apparent Km (more substrate needed to reach half Vmax) but does not affect Vmax because at high substrate concentrations the inhibitor can be outcompeted. Other options are incorrect: noncompetitive inhibitors decrease Vmax with no change in Km, and uncompetitive inhibitors decrease both Km and Vmax.",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "topic": "Enzymes",
        "subject": "Biochemistry"
